tfig - terminal figures
=======================

Read pairs of numbers from stdin and draw a scatter plot on the
terminal. Omitted bounds fit the data exactly. Given bounds may be
fractional and are inclusive. -s takes one character that is one column
wide, including a UTF-8 character such as '•'. A single sample is drawn
in the middle of the plot. -w and -h must be between 1 and 10000.

Usage Example
-------------

$ seq 1 5 | awk '{print $1, $1*$1}' | tfig -x 0 -X 5 -y 0 -Y 5 -h 5 -w 5 -s '?'

Expected Output
---------------

|  ?  
|     
|     
| ?   
|     
+-----
